# FDD 09 review — "9 - Professional Practice Review (PPR) (9.1-9.6)" (Features 9.1-9.5;
# 9.6 "Document Upload" is a header label folded into 9.1.1's own acceptance criteria, not a
# separately-numbered feature anywhere in the document). Ingested per
# abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md against the mied-v3 Professional Practices graph
# (profpractice-domain.ttl / profpractice-permissions.ttl / profpractice-api.ttl /
# profpractice-sequences.ttl, all loaded together), plus a cross-domain check against
# reporting-capability.ttl/-api.ttl/-permissions.ttl and documents-api.ttl for Feature 9.5 and
# the disclosure-attachment sub-flows respectively. Per CONVENTIONS.md's own note, the source
# folder is named "profpractice" (no trailing s) but sd:identifier/prefix are
# "profpractices"/`profp:` — kept exactly as the existing convention states; no new prefix
# invented.
#
# UNUSUAL FINDING WORTH FLAGGING UP FRONT: profpractice-domain.ttl's own header comment and
# several of its sd:notes already cite "BRD 9.1.19", "BRD 9.1.20", "BRD 9.1.6", "BRD 9.1.7",
# "BRD 9.1.8", "BRD 9.1.9b", and "BRD 9.4.1" by number — i.e. the mied-v3 Phase 1 conversion of
# this domain was ALREADY written with this exact FDD open next to it. This pass is therefore
# unusually confirmatory rather than exploratory for most numbered items: most of Feature
# 9.1-9.4's stories already have a close, sometimes verbatim, match in the domain model. This is
# noted rather than treated as suspicious — it explains why the Satisfied count below is high
# relative to other FDD folders in this batch, and it does NOT mean every item was rubber-stamped
# (9.2.2 is rejected outright per an explicit reviewer comment; several items are satisfied only
# partially, with the gap named in sd:notes; Feature 9.5 turns out to be satisfied almost
# entirely by the separate Reporting bounded context, not by profpractice's own artifacts).
#
# Structure of the document and what's used as the Requirement unit:
# - A "Business Specifications" prose section and a 42-row "High Level Scenarios" paraphrase
#   table both restate the same disclosure/PPR-response/worklist/admin behaviors at coarser
#   grain than the Addendum below — both are skipped per CONVENTIONS.md as duplicative of the
#   Addendum, which has the FDD's own real Feature/story numbering (9.1.1-9.1.8, an unnumbered
#   Feature-9.2 intro story, 9.2.1-9.2.4, 9.3.1-9.3.6, 9.4.1, 9.5.1-9.5.4) and per-story
#   acceptance criteria the paraphrase table lacks.
# - Feature 9.2's own intro line ("As a Credentialing Admin, I want to manage all the email
#   templates...") is never given a number anywhere in the document, unlike every other story —
#   modeled below with a synthetic ID (profp:Req_09_2_0), same convention FDD 29's pass used for
#   its own un-numbered-but-real Business-Specifications items.
# - Feature 9.6 ("Document Upload"), named only in the Feature-9.1 heading's own title
#   ("Feature: 9.1 Individual User Disclosure & 9.6 Document Upload"), is never given its own
#   numbered story anywhere — document upload is folded entirely into 9.1.1's acceptance
#   criteria (the Upload field, the Select-Type-per-document dropdown, deleting an uploaded file
#   before submission). Not modeled as a separate Requirement for a feature number that has no
#   actual content of its own.
#
# Comments (147 total across comments.xml/commentsExtended.xml/commentsExtensible.xml/
# commentsIds.xml, several duplicated verbatim across two review passes — 2025-10 through
# 2025-12, then again 2026-01 and 2026-03 — evidently the same open items were carried forward
# and re-flagged rather than resolved in between). Two threads surfaced findings substantial
# enough to promote to standalone Annotations (9.2.2's outright rejection; 9.1.8's
# computed-vs-stored-flag architecture mismatch). A representative sample of the many
# "To be changed"/"To be confirmed"/"To be defined" single-word placeholder comments (dozens,
# mostly Sinha (DTMB-Contractor) editorial placeholders from the 2025-10/11 pass, largely
# resolved by the later Dontje/Groom replies) are folded into the relevant Requirement's own
# sd:notes rather than transcribed one-by-one, per this project's dedup convention — the
# repetition itself (a heavily-iterated, still-being-revised document even past its nominal
# 08/01/2025 sign-off date) is the finding, stated once here rather than per-comment.
#
# Tracked changes: not separately reconstructed as a diff (per CONVENTIONS.md); one deleted
# paragraph inside 9.3.3's acceptance criteria (comment 728676430, "Rap Back Reviewer
# responsibility; Removed from PPR") could not be recovered as literal text since the paragraph
# itself is now empty in document.xml — the comment's intent is clear enough (a RapBack-specific
# sub-capability was scoped out of the PPR Reviewer role) to note in Req_09_3_3's own sd:notes
# without fabricating the removed wording.
#
# Wireframes: document.xml embeds ~34 screenshots via <w:drawing>, but NONE carry a "Wireframe N"
# caption the way FDD 29's did — they're inserted inline next to the story they illustrate with
# no caption at all. A packaging quirk matching FDD 29's own "packaging quirk" note is present
# here too: nine of the images (image20.png-image28.png) are each referenced TWICE, once via a
# normal numbered rId near their apparent authoring position (9.1.4/9.1.7/9.2.4/9.3.1/9.3.3/9.5.1)
# and again via a second, large-integer rId with an absolute "/media/imageN.png" target near an
# EARLIER story (9.1.1/9.1.3/9.1.4/9.3.5) — i.e. the same ~28 distinct images are effectively
# reused/duplicated across roughly 34 embed sites, not 34 independent screenshots. Six
# representative images were extracted and actually viewed (confirmed by viewing, not assumed
# from position) to wireframes/: the Business-Specifications-section "Professional Practice
# questions" annual-review form (image1 -> wireframe-01), the "Uploaded Documents" list/upload
# panel (image2 -> wireframe-02), the reviewer-facing "Professional Practices Review" detail
# screen with Action dropdown, PPR Admin Flag / PPR Additional Review Flag toggles, and
# External/Internal Remarks (image3 -> wireframe-03) — a close match for 9.3.1/9.3.5 — the "My
# Disclosure History" Responses/Disclosures-tab screen with search, filter, and download icons
# (image19 -> wireframe-04) — a close match for 9.1.4/9.1.5/9.1.6 — the "Professional Practice
# Review" worklist with Unresolved/Resolved tabs and a Type column literally showing "Yearly",
# "Disclosure", and "Rapback" values side by side (image22 -> wireframe-05) — direct visual
# confirmation of comment 136's point that the worklist is NOT self-disclosures-only — and the
# admin hamburger menu showing "Report Management" as its own top-level nav item alongside
# "Business Rules"/"Communication Management"/"Questions Management"/"System Reports" (image26 ->
# wireframe-06) — visual support for treating Feature 9.5's admin report-catalog management as a
# cross-cutting capability rather than PPR-specific (see the Feature 9.5 notes below). The
# remaining ~22 embed sites were not individually viewed; per CONVENTIONS.md's depth-calibration
# guidance, the six sampled span early/mid/late document position and cover the visually distinct
# screen types (citizen self-disclosure form, admin/reviewer worklist, disclosure history,
# navigation chrome) — nothing suggests the unsampled sites are a materially different, unseen
# feature rather than more of the same screens repeated near their other authoring sites.
#
# CROSS-DOMAIN CHECK (Feature 9.5, per this review's own reading of the domain model before
# writing anything): Feature 9.5's own reviewer comments (on 9.5.2 and 9.5.4) say "This should be
# moved to #2 Reports" / "...will use the MiEdWorkforce standards defined in #2", echoing this
# FDD's own Dependencies section ("supported...by the business specifications defined in
# Reporting (2)"). Checked against the actual graph rather than taken on faith: reporting-
# capability.ttl/-api.ttl/-permissions.ttl (a real, independently-converted domain in this same
# mied-v3 batch) already models almost exactly what 9.5.1/9.5.2 describe — rpt:ReportDefinition
# Aggregate (workspace/report IDs, permission-key gating, per-domain association, Active/Inactive
# status) plus admin CRUD operations (rpt:Op_AdminCreateReport, rpt:Op_AdminListReports,
# rpt:Op_AdminUpdateReport, rpt:Op_AdminUpdateReportStatus — the last one matching 9.5.2's
# Active/Inactive toggle almost operation-for-operation) and view-side operations
# (rpt:Op_ListReports, rpt:Op_GetReport, rpt:Op_GenerateEmbedToken) matching 9.5.3. All four 9.5.x
# stories are therefore modeled below as SATISFIED, but by rpt: (Reporting) nodes rather than by
# any profpractice-owned artifact — profpractice's own profp:Seq_GeneratePPRComplianceReport /
# profp:Op_GetPprReportData supply only the PPR-specific data feed a rendered report would query,
# not the report-catalog admin/embed machinery itself. This is the one place this pass disagrees
# with a literal reading of "which domain does this FDD file live under" — the content is real
# and accounted for, just cross-domain, exactly as the FDD's own dependency note and reviewer
# comments already say.
#
# Feature 9.1's attachment sub-flow (upload/label/delete-before-submission) is satisfied via
# docs:Op_RequestDocumentUpload (a real mied-v3 Documents operation, same good match FDD 29's own
# pass found for its own upload story — not the placeholder stub the pre-mied-v3 pass had to use).

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix profp: <urn:solutiondesign:instance:profpractices:> .
@prefix comm:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:> .
@prefix docs:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:> .
@prefix rpt:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:> .
@prefix ext:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:external:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

profp:Fdd09Doc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/09 - Professional Practices/9 - Professional Practice.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Covers Features 9.1-9.5 (the document's own subtitle: '9 - Professional Practice Review (PPR) (9.1-9.6)', though no 9.6-numbered story exists anywhere — see this file's header). Author(s) Beth Dontje / Caitlin Groom / Kate Boswell Gallagher; approved by Dontje (MDE) and Groom (CEPI) both 08/01/2025 per the sign-off table — but the comment threads (comments.xml/commentsExtended.xml/commentsExtensible.xml/commentsIds.xml) contain dated entries from 2025-10 through 2026-03, well past that nominal approval date, meaning the document continued to be actively revised long after its sign-off. Not resolved here; noted so the sign-off table isn't read as 'nothing changed after this' (same caveat FDD 29's own pass raised for its document)." .

profp:Wireframe1 a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/09-professional-practices/wireframes/wireframe-01-annual-ppr-review-questions.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Professional Practice questions' form — two Yes/No misdemeanor/felony questions, an inline conviction table (Type/Conviction Date/Description) with edit/delete icons, a second 'Regarding any professional credentials...' block (suspended/revoked, surrendered/nullified, pending action questions) with its own conviction table, Cancel/Save actions. Matches the Business-Specifications-section Annual PPR Review question set (9.1.3) closely, including the exact question wording." ;
    sd:definedIn profp:Fdd09Doc .
profp:Wireframe2 a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/09-professional-practices/wireframes/wireframe-02-uploaded-documents.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Uploaded Documents' table (File name/Description/uploaded by/Date/Size, edit+delete icons per row) plus an 'Upload Additional Documents' panel (Browse/Upload, 1MB max for PDF files stated inline). Corroborates 9.1.1's upload/delete-before-submission acceptance criteria and Rule_AttachmentManagement's soft-delete framing." ;
    sd:definedIn profp:Fdd09Doc .
profp:Wireframe3 a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/09-professional-practices/wireframes/wireframe-03-ppr-reviewer-detail-flags.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: reviewer-facing 'Professional Practices Review' detail screen for one educator (Name/Unique ID/SSN/Gender header, prior-conviction table with MDE Remarks column, credential-suspension/surrender/pending-action Yes/No block), an Action dropdown pre-populated with the full disclosure status list (PPR Hold, PPR Document Hold, Reviewed - Felony/Listed/No Action Required/Non-Enumerated/Misdemeanor/Arraignment) matching profp:DiscState_* one-for-one, PPR Admin Flag and PPR Additional Review Flag toggles shown directly on this same screen (not a separate profile page), and External Remarks (labelled 'visible to the educator') / Internal Remarks fields side by side. Direct visual confirmation of 9.3.1's Actions dropdown and 9.3.5's flag-toggle placement — see Req_09_3_5's own notes on the still-open 'where do these flags actually live' review thread, since this wireframe answers it one way (inline on the disclosure record) while the comment thread treats that as unresolved." ;
    sd:definedIn profp:Fdd09Doc .
profp:Wireframe4 a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/09-professional-practices/wireframes/wireframe-04-my-disclosure-history.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'My Disclosure History' citizen-facing screen, Responses/Disclosures tabs, a search box, and both a filter icon and a download icon in the table's top-right corner. Table columns shown (Submission Date/Type/New Disclosures/Status) match 9.1.4's Responses-tab column list. Direct visual confirmation that 9.1.4 (view history), 9.1.5 (download), and 9.1.6 (filter) are three facets of this one screen, not three separate screens." ;
    sd:definedIn profp:Fdd09Doc .
profp:Wireframe5 a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/09-professional-practices/wireframes/wireframe-05-ppr-review-worklist.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: 'Professional Practice Review' worklist, Unresolved/Resolved tabs, search-by-name-or-ID, filter and download icons, and a results table whose Type column shows 'Yearly', 'Disclosure', and 'Rapback' values across different rows for the SAME columns (Application #/Name/Unique ID/Certificate Type/Type/School District/Has Conviction?/Status). Direct visual confirmation of comment 136's point (the worklist spans self-disclosures, annual PPR responses, AND Rap Back records, not self-disclosures alone) and of 9.3.1's Unresolved/Resolved tab structure." ;
    sd:definedIn profp:Fdd09Doc .
profp:Wireframe6 a sd:SourceDocument ; sd:docType "wireframe" ;
    sd:section "abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/09-professional-practices/wireframes/wireframe-06-admin-hamburger-menu.png" ;
    sd:notes "Confirmed by viewing: the admin hamburger menu listing 'Report Management' as its own top-level item, alongside 'Business Rules', 'Communication Management', 'Position Management', 'Credential Management', 'Questions Management', 'System Users & Roles', and 'System Reports' — none of them scoped under a 'Professional Practice' heading. Visual support (not proof) for this pass's read that Feature 9.5's report-catalog admin page is generic/cross-cutting UI chrome rather than a PPR-specific build item — see the Feature 9.5 cross-domain note in this file's header." ;
